{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-confinement-level-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:confinement-level-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the confinement level","tags":["existence","confinement","filtration"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementLevel.nonempty","text":"confinement-level-exists.md","leanSource":"confinement-level-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:confinement-level-exists\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Existence of the confinement level</em></p>\n<p><em>For any closed braid <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> with normal form <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_w \\in H_{n(K)}(q)</code> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> in the generic locus, the confinement level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ell(K, q)</code> exists and is finite.</em></p>\n"}
